    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1139">

                <pb facs="1113" n="947" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg947"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.011/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thurston, in charge
                        of American interests, to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-19T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Am advised reformed Article 33 relating to foreigners will soon be passed upon at
                    Querétaro. To-day press publishes conservative and drastic forms submitted both
                    containing a clause as to foreigners renouncing citizenship rights and up to
                    acquiring certain classes of property in Mexico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
